    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "x-api-key",
              "value": "={{ $credentials.anthropicApi.apiKey }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "anthropic-version",
              "value": "2023-06-01"
            },
            {
              "name": "content-type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ]
        },
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({\n  model: \"claude-sonnet-4-6\",\n  max_tokens: 1500,\n  system: \"You are GFIN's content director rewriting a blog essay into a native LinkedIn post. Rules: (1) Re-architect for LinkedIn behavior — hook-first, short paragraphs, one argument, plain language. Do NOT summarize or trim the blog paragraphs verbatim. (2) Map the essay to exactly one of these 8 pillars: REFRAME, MYTH-BUST, BEHIND-THE-DATA, PROOF, AUDIENCE-ED, CAPACITY-BUILD, DEADLINE-WATCH, SERIES. (3) Assign exactly one audience: NONPROFIT, FAITH-BASED, GOVERNMENT, ENTERPRISE, or ALL (only if genuinely cross-audience). (4) Use asset-framing — never savior language, never deficit framing. AI (ARTEMIS) is infrastructure, never the hero; humans decide and are the accountable submitter. (5) Never invent statistics, client names, funders, deadlines, or results — if the source article states a number without a cited source, mark it '[VERIFIED STAT NEEDED]'. (6) CTA must be: Take the Funding Readiness Assessment (Phase 1 awareness — this is the current phase). (7) Set needs_review true if the draft contains any statistic/dollar figure, targets a FAITH-BASED audience, or names a specific funder/deadline/client. Respond with ONLY valid JSON, no prose, no markdown fences, matching this schema: {\\\"pillar\\\": string, \\\"audience\\\": string, \\\"hook_direct\\\": string, \\\"hook_contrarian\\\": string, \\\"hook_human\\\": string, \\\"linkedin_draft\\\": string, \\\"needs_review\\\": boolean, \\\"needs_review_reasons\\\": string[]}\",\n  messages: [\n    { role: \"user\", content: \"Source article title: \" + $json.title + \"\\n\\nSource article body:\\n\" + $json.bodyText }\n  ]\n}) }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "10a46fb1-f02c-4d72-9a64-feb18366b357",
      "name": "Claude Rewrite for LinkedIn",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        1952,
        224
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Parse Claude's JSON response and attach the required 4-tag family.\nconst apiResponse = items[0].json;\nconst textBlock = (apiResponse.content || []).find(b => b.type === 'text');\nlet parsed;\ntry {\n  parsed = JSON.parse((textBlock && textBlock.text) || '{}');\n} catch (e) {\n  parsed = {\n    pillar: 'UNKNOWN',\n    audience: 'UNKNOWN',\n    hook_direct: '', hook_contrarian: '', hook_human: '',\n    linkedin_draft: '',\n    needs_review: true,\n    needs_review_reasons: ['Failed to parse model output — manual review required.']\n  };\n}\n\nconst article = $node['Loop Over New Articles'].json;\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    ...parsed,\n    title: article.title,\n    source_url: article.url,\n    slug: article.slug,\n    date_published: article.date,\n    tags: {\n      source: 'REPURPOSED-BLOG',\n      pillar: parsed.pillar,\n      audience: parsed.audience,\n      phase: 'AWARENESS' // update when campaign moves to Phase 2/3\n    }\n  }\n}];"
      },
